  "thermal_method": "Pedley and Marshall Tables 9 and 11 give the YO Gibbs-energy function -(G°-H°298)/T and enthalpy function H°-H°298. Entropy is derived as S°=-(G°-H°298)/T+(H°-H°298)/T; Cp is the centered 100 K finite difference of the printed enthalpy function (one-sided at the fitted range endpoints). Values are transcribed or derived at 298.15 and 1200-3000 K; standard pressure 1 bar.",
  "source_note": "Pedley and Marshall Table 5 selects ΔfH°(298.15 K) = -46 ± 10 kJ/mol (reported as -11.0 ± 2.5 kcal/mol); Table 5 gives D0 = 715 ± 11 kJ/mol. Their section 5.3 selects YO from compatible vaporization and metathetical reactions. The reference is elemental. Thermal functions use the printed Tables 9 and 11, rather than a new partition-function evaluation.",
